course: dictionary
lesson: 3568
title: Fertilizer: food for plants
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Plants make some of their own food using sunlight, water and air, but they also need minerals from the soil to grow strong. A fertilizer is something we add to soil to give plants extra nutrients, which are the food plants need to grow better.
explain: Look at the context: «Bat droppings, called guano, pile into huge heaps that feed cave beetles and worms, and guano was once mined as valuable fertilizer.» The word valuable tells you people wanted it, because it helped crops grow. Fertilizer is useful, not rubbish.
explain: Fertilizer can be natural, like manure and compost, or made in factories as chemical fertilizer. In British English the spelling is fertiliser, but the meaning is the same. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Fertilizer is a substance added to soil to help plants grow.
fact: Plant nutrients include nitrogen, phosphorus and potassium.
fact: Natural fertilizers include manure and compost, and some are made in factories.
fact: «Guano» is bat droppings, and it was once mined as valuable fertilizer.
fact: Too much fertilizer can run off into rivers and cause pollution, and it must be kept away from children and pets.
exercise: What is a fertilizer? | A kind of beetle that lives in soil | A tool for digging holes | A type of rock found in caves | *Something added to soil to give plants food
exercise: Which of these is a natural fertilizer? | Sand | Glass bottle | *Manure | Plastic bag
exercise: Which of these is a plant nutrient? | Plastic | Paint | Glue | *Nitrogen
test: In «guano was once mined as valuable fertilizer», what does valuable mean? | *Worth a lot, useful | Cheap and easy to find | Very dirty | Hidden deep underground
test: Why should fertilizer be kept away from children and pets? | It smells like sweets | *It can harm them | It is too heavy to lift | It makes them grow taller
exam: What can happen when fertilizer runs into rivers? | It is cleaned by fish | *It can cause pollution | It makes the water freeze | It turns into soil
